{"assets":["/statement-assets/710aab82127574b7d3184ac1566d2609db197cf76b16baaa6b24ce11bab93297.png","/statement-assets/de5f2154d027d598838c2ec71ca4a45c7207e041cb513d59507ed1571cd42516.png","/statement-assets/b76d4211703e5f04fa69ae1851a359d5931558bcfdb488c2604350546dbc0705.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1556","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. Gates to Another World"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/710aab82127574b7d3184ac1566d2609db197cf76b16baaa6b24ce11bab93297.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As mentioned previously William really likes playing video games. In one of his favorite games, the player character is in a universe where every planet is designated by a binary number from $$$0$$$ to $$$2^n - 1$$$. On each planet, there are gates that allow the player to move from planet $$$i$$$ to planet $$$j$$$ if the binary representations of $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ differ in exactly one bit."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"William wants to test you and see how you can handle processing the following queries in this game universe:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Destroy planets with numbers from $$$l$$$ to $$$r$$$ inclusively. These planets cannot be moved to anymore."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Figure out if it is possible to reach planet $$$b$$$ from planet $$$a$$$ using some number of planetary gates. It is guaranteed that the planets $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ are not destroyed. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 50$$$, $$$1 \\leq m \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^4$$$), which are the number of bits in binary representation of each planets' designation and the number of queries, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$m$$$ lines contains a query of two types:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"block l r"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — query for destruction of planets with numbers from $$$l$$$ to $$$r$$$ inclusively ($$$0 \\le l \\le r \\lt 2^n$$$). It's guaranteed that no planet will be destroyed twice."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ask a b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — query for reachability between planets $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ ($$$0 \\le a, b \\lt 2^n$$$). It's guaranteed that planets $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ hasn't been destroyed yet."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each query of type "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ask"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" you must output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in a new line, if it is possible to reach planet $$$b$$$ from planet $$$a$$$ and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise (without quotation marks)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3\nask 0 7\nblock 3 6\nask 0 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 10\nblock 12 26\nask 44 63\nblock 32 46\nask 1 54\nblock 27 30\nask 10 31\nask 11 31\nask 49 31\nblock 31 31\nask 2 51\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n1\n0\n0\n1\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first example test can be visualized in the following way:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/de5f2154d027d598838c2ec71ca4a45c7207e041cb513d59507ed1571cd42516.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Response to a query "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ask 0 7"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is positive."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next after query "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"block 3 6"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the graph will look the following way (destroyed vertices are highlighted):"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b76d4211703e5f04fa69ae1851a359d5931558bcfdb488c2604350546dbc0705.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Response to a query "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ask 0 7"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is negative, since any path from vertex $$$0$$$ to vertex $$$7$$$ must go through one of the destroyed vertices."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"1556G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1556/problem/G"}